  _longDescription: The Lantock-class frigate project was a rejected proposal to
    replace the Raines-class frigates. The Lantock-class frigates were to be equipped
    with two medium-sized missile launchers and four small defensive mounts. The
    design features integrated missile support systems at the expense of artillery
    armament. Preserved prototypes were hastily pressed into service following the
    Harper Incident.
